ChefIQ Wireless Meat Thermometer Probe Analysis tool

Purpose: To be able to look at previous cooks and determine the best temperatures, times, and techniques for smoking meats

What it does:
 - Upload your Data from the ChefIQ app
    - Go to "More" > "Cooking History"
    - Click on the cook youd like to upload, hit export graph
    - Save the graph to files
    - Open "https://collapse-quantum-lard.ngrok-free.dev"
    - Name and upload your data
    - Look at your graph and the temperature delta to analyze your ambient temperature stability and how evenly your meat cooked

Next Steps:
   - Create Page to look through past cooks. Pull up graphs for individual cooks
   - Brainstorm analysis techniques. What info do I want to know
      - Color in fat-rendering portion of time-temp graph
      - Add in weight (collecting data on how long it took what weight to cook)
      - Stall duration. Analyzing change in temp/time
      - Optimal pull-off temperature based on previous cooks (how high they continued to rise)
   - Use a more interactive graphing software. Be able to zoom in and out